// Campaign chapter 2 (B-025): hold the line. The mission player survives
// 3600 ticks (two minutes of game time) against the scripted Alpha's waves
// — B-017's survive kind carrying the chapter, with B-015's explored fog
// preset so the battlefield starts revealed (the fog preset changes the
// filter's initial state only — derived, unhashed, FD-8; the per-tick
// vision pass marks live sight on top exactly as always).
//
// The optional protect objective (B-017) is fail-only state for the end
// screen: it never completes, never gates — if the command center falls
// while the survivors hold on, the mission can still be won, and the
// record shows the base was lost doing it. Victory is reachable through
// the required survive objective alone (the loader's victory-reachability
// gate), so the protect flag is optional, not required.
//
// The Alpha opponent runs its own default pacing — feel tuning is the
// owner's (the playtest instruments, STANDING_ORDERS §8), not content
// this brief presumes.
(
    schema_version: 1,
    id: "crossroads_02",
    display_name: "Hold the Line",
    map: "crossroads_64",
    faction: "legion",
    rules: "alpha",
    fog_preset: Some("Explored"),
    objectives: [
        // Survive the window — 3600 ticks is twenty times the loader's
        // 300-tick floor: real play, not a vacuous tick count.
        (
            kind: "Survive",
            parameters: Survive(( ticks: 3600 )),
            optional: false,
        ),
        // Keep the command center alive — optional, fail-only: the end
        // screen's honesty line, never the match outcome.
        (
            kind: "Protect",
            parameters: Protect(( kind: "command_center" )),
            optional: true,
        ),
    ],
)
